From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] build/config: do not treat warnings as errors

The engine adds -Werror unconditionally, and riscv64 builds this tree
with oe-core's native clang rather than the clang bundled in the SDK's
buildtools, because CLANG_PATH:riscv64 points at the native toolchain.
That toolchain is far newer than the one upstream tests against, so each
clang release turns another diagnostic on in vendored third-party
sources:

  double-conversion/src/bignum.cc:49:12: error: unused function template
    'BitSize' [-Werror,-Wunused-template]

  abseil-cpp/absl/synchronization/mutex.h:602:68: error:
    'lifetime_capture_by(this)' is deprecated [-Werror,-Wdeprecated-attributes]

Disabling them one at a time only defers the next one, and none of this
is code the layer can fix. Drop -Werror instead; the warnings still
print.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific toolchain combination]
Signed-off-by: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
---
diff --git a/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn b/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
--- a/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -740,7 +740,13 @@ if (is_win) {
     "-Wno-unused-parameter",  # Unused function parameters.
   ]
 
-  if (!is_qnx) {
+  # -Werror removed: meta-flutter builds this tree for riscv64 with oe-core's
+  # native clang rather than the clang bundled in the SDK's buildtools, and
+  # that toolchain is far newer than the one upstream tests against. Each
+  # release turns another diagnostic on in vendored third-party sources --
+  # -Wunused-template in double-conversion, -Wdeprecated-attributes in
+  # abseil -- none of which is code this layer can fix. Warnings still print.
+  if (false) {
     default_warning_flags += [
       "-Werror",  # Warnings as errors.
     ]
